WEBVTT`r`n`r`n1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:07.018
Let me show you how Arbiter turns an AI-generated change into a decision you can actually trust.
2
00:00:07.018 --> 00:00:11.953
Right here. we have one authoritative verdict: ready to approve.

3
00:00:11.953 --> 00:00:17.135
The evidence is verified... but notice. the human decision is still pending.

4
00:00:17.135 --> 00:00:24.101
Now. when we open Change. Arbiter connects the original authorization to an immutable Git candidate.

5
00:00:24.101 --> 00:00:29.466
We can see exactly what changed—and whether that change stayed inside its approved scope.

6
00:00:29.466 --> 00:00:32.408
Validation is where this gets interesting.

7
00:00:32.408 --> 00:00:33.736
Run One failed.

8
00:00:33.736 --> 00:00:36.041
That result never disappears.

9
00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:42.005
After remediation. Run Two performs the full validation again... and passes.

10
00:00:42.005 --> 00:00:46.549
We can move between both outcomes. so the audit story stays intact.

11
00:00:46.549 --> 00:00:56.341
Open any check. and the conclusion becomes explainable: what we expected. what Arbiter actually observed. and which evidence supports the result.

12
00:00:56.341 --> 00:01:01.458
Over in Evidence. every artifact is persisted and traceable.

13
00:01:01.458 --> 00:01:11.471
Open a record and you get its producer. source. portable path. SHA-256 digest. and independently verified integrity.

14
00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:21.627
History then reconstructs the whole trust loop—from authorization and baseline. through failure and remediation. all the way to readiness.

15
00:01:21.627 --> 00:01:23.398
And here's the key boundary.

16
00:01:23.398 --> 00:01:25.625
Arbiter has done the validation.

17
00:01:25.625 --> 00:01:29.244
The exact candidate is eligible for approval.

18
00:01:29.244 --> 00:01:31.093
But automation stops here.

19
00:01:31.093 --> 00:01:34.804
A named human still owns the final decision.

20
00:01:34.804 --> 00:01:40.768
We can review the action. confirm the candidate. and deliberately approve—or step away.

21
00:01:40.768 --> 00:01:48.281
That separation is the point: independent assurance. durable evidence. and human control where it matters.
